&lt;h2&gt;About the team&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking an experienced Engineering Manager to lead our Developer Experience team within the Connection organization. This team owns Alloy&#39;s external-facing integration surface - the APIs, webhooks, and tooling that developers and partners use to connect with Alloy and build on top of our platform.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you will lead a team responsible for the systems and experiences that make Alloy easy to integrate with: our Events API, Outgoing Webhooks Service, partnership data feeds, external developer documentation, and the integrations that power Alloy&#39;s channel partner ecosystem. You will own the technical and strategic vision for how data flows in and out of Alloy at scale, and how external developers experience the platform - from first API call to production.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Alloy operates in a hybrid-work environment. We look to foster collaboration and community by having our local employees onsite three days a week.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll be doing&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Engineering Manager&#39;s primary responsibility is their team. You will balance three key areas: recruiting and growing great engineers, supporting each person&#39;s development, and partnering with product and stakeholders to ship high-quality, high-impact work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;As the Engineering Manager, you will:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead, develop, and mentor a team of engineers through weekly 1:1s, career conversations, and hands-on technical guidance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the roadmap and delivery for Alloy&#39;s developer-facing infrastructure — APIs, webhooks, data ingestion, and outbound data flows - ensuring reliability, scalability, and a great developer experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with product, design, partnerships, and customer-facing teams to shape what gets built and why.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive technical strategy for the team&#39;s systems, including API design standards, event delivery guarantees, and integration patterns used by external developers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track and improve engineering health using DORA metrics and team-level KPIs; establish release and monitoring standards that keep quality high.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recruit and hire strong engineers; own onboarding and ramp for new team members.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate clearly across the organization — surface risks, resolve blockers, and keep stakeholders aligned on progress and trade-offs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we’re looking for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for an Engineering Manager who has built and led teams working on developer-facing products, APIs, or platform infrastructure. An ideal candidate has::&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years in engineering with at least 3 years in an engineering leadership role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong background in developer experience, API platform engineering, or developer tooling - you have shipped products that external developers integrate with and build on top of.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep familiarity with API design and HTTP/event-based integration patterns (REST, webhooks, async messaging); you can credibly lead technical discussions on API contract design, delivery guarantees, and integration reliability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of building and shipping high-quality systems at scale, with clear accountability for outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical fluency in modern backend stacks - strong with TypeScript/Node.js; comfortable reviewing code, debugging production issues, and contributing to architectural decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with external partners or customers on integration work; you understand what makes a platform easy (or hard) to integrate with.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading sprint planning, goal-based project tracking, and cross-functional delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills; able to translate technical complexity for non-technical stakeholders and advocate for the team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience recruiting, hiring, and onboarding engineers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A servant-leader mindset - you lead by removing obstacles, pointing people in the right direction, and investing in the people around you.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be local to New York City and attend the office 3-4 days per week.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in high-growth product companies or startups.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in fintech, financial services, or other regulated industries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re a lean team, so your impact will be felt immediately, and opportunities will grow as the company scales up. If this all sounds like a good fit for you, why not join us?&lt;/p&gt;
