&lt;li&gt;Shape technical direction across the frontend stack through architecture, standards, and durable shared patterns&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and improve both shared frontend foundations and customer-facing product surfaces&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with engineering, design, and product to turn broad needs into simple, scalable solutions with meaningful user and business impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Raise the quality bar across teams through strong technical judgment, clear documentation, and improvements to developer experience, reliability, and engineering practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help shape effective use of AI and agentic engineering workflows in frontend development to improve leverage, quality, and delivery speed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we’re looking for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re a senior frontend engineer with 8+ years of experience, deep fundamentals in JavaScript or TypeScript, modern HTML and CSS, and experience building complex web applications with a modern framework such as React&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’ve led large, complex frontend or platform initiatives and influenced technical direction beyond your immediate team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have strong engineering judgment and know how to balance user experience, product needs, maintainability, operational excellence, and delivery speed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re comfortable operating in ambiguity and can turn loosely defined problem spaces into clear technical direction and execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You bring strong product and business context, and use it to influence prioritization and improve customer outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You use AI-enabled tools thoughtfully and responsibly, with a high quality bar and without outsourcing core engineering thinking&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re a lean team, so your impact will be felt immediately, and opportunities will grow as the company scales up. If this all sounds like a good fit for you, why not join us?&lt;/p&gt;
